"assets:broker1","DEF","","","0","","$30","0","0","0.0","","","$20","1209.5"

# ** 33. A fully disposed account is hidden by default, but its realised
# gain and cashflows are still included in the totals row's RGain and XIRR,
# which cover all lots within the query. #2693, #2769
<
commodity ABC ; lots:
commodity DEF ; lots:

2020-01-01 buy ABC in broker1
     assets:cash         -$10
     assets:broker1      1 ABC

2020-01-01 buy DEF in broker2
     assets:cash         -$10
     assets:broker2      1 DEF

P 2020-05-05 ABC $15
P 2020-05-05 DEF $30

2020-06-05 sell all of broker2s DEF
     assets:broker2       -1 DEF
     assets:cash          $30
$ hledger -f- holdings -e 2026-07-01
Holdings on 2026-06-30

                ||       Date   Age  Units  Avg cost  Unit price  Total cost  Total value  Weight  UGain  UGain%  RGain    XIRR 
================++==============================================================================================================
 assets:broker1 || 2020-01-01  6.5y  1 ABC       $10         $15         $10          $15  100.0%     $5   50.0%           6.4% 
----------------++--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
                ||                   1 ABC       $10                     $10          $15  100.0%     $5   50.0%    $20  159.3% 

# ** 34. -E shows the fully disposed account as a zero-units row, and the
# totals then include its realised gain and cashflows. #2693
$ hledger -f- holdings -e 2026-07-01 -E
Holdings on 2026-06-30

                ||       Date   Age  Units  Avg cost  Unit price  Total cost  Total value  Weight  UGain  UGain%  RGain     XIRR 
================++===============================================================================================================
 assets:broker1 || 2020-01-01  6.5y  1 ABC       $10         $15         $10          $15  100.0%     $5   50.0%            6.4% 
 assets:broker2 ||                   0 DEF                   $30                       $0    0.0%                   $20  1209.5% 
----------------++---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
                ||                   1 ABC       $10                     $10          $15  100.0%     $5   50.0%    $20   159.3% 

# ** 35. Lots are valued individually, each in its own cost commodity;
# a row's Unit price, Total value and UGain aggregate them, showing multiple amounts
# when the lots' cost commodities differ (like Total cost).
<
commodity AAPL  ; lots:

2026-01-15 buy in dollars
    assets:us:stocks    10 AAPL @ $50
    assets:us:cash

2026-02-01 buy in euros
    assets:eu:stocks    10 AAPL @ €45
    assets:eu:cash

P 2026-03-31 AAPL $72
P 2026-03-31 AAPL €60
$ hledger -f- holdings -e 2026-04-01
Holdings on 2026-03-31

                  ||       Date  Age    Units  Avg cost  Unit price  Total cost  Total value  Weight       UGain  UGain%  RGain    XIRR 
==================++====================================================================================================================
 assets:eu:stocks || 2026-02-01  58d  10 AAPL       €45         €60        €450         €600                €150   33.3%         512.1% 
 assets:us:stocks || 2026-01-15  75d  10 AAPL       $50         $72        $500         $720                $220   44.0%         490.5% 
------------------++--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
                  ||                  20 AAPL                        $500, €450   $720, €600          $220, €150                        

# ** 36. So values and value totals do not depend on how lots are
# grouped into rows: aggregating with --depth changes no numbers.
$ hledger -f- holdings -e 2026-04-01 --depth 1
Holdings on 2026-03-31

        || Date  Age    Units  Avg cost  Unit price  Total cost  Total value  Weight       UGain  UGain%  RGain  XIRR 
========++============================================================================================================
 assets ||            20 AAPL              $72, €60  $500, €450   $720, €600          $220, €150                      
--------++------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
        ||            20 AAPL                        $500, €450   $720, €600          $220, €150                      

# ** 37. Likewise when regrouping with --pivot.
$ hledger -f- holdings -e 2026-04-01 --pivot cur:acct --depth 1
Holdings on 2026-03-31

      || Date  Age    Units  Avg cost  Unit price  Total cost  Total value  Weight       UGain  UGain%  RGain  XIRR 
======++============================================================================================================
 AAPL ||            20 AAPL              $72, €60  $500, €450   $720, €600          $220, €150                      
------++------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
      ||            20 AAPL                        $500, €450   $720, €600          $220, €150                      
# ** 38. An AVERAGE account's Avg cost and Total cost columns show the pool's
# running average cost, computed from the lot postings' cost basis
# annotations (the costless lot subaccount names carry no cost).
# Here: (10*$10 + 10*$30 - 5*$20) / 15 = $20; a disposal doesn't
# change the average, and RGain uses it.
<
commodity AAPL  ; lots:AVERAGE

2026-01-01 buy cheap
    assets:cash     -$100
    assets:broker    10 AAPL @ $10

2026-02-01 buy dear
    assets:cash     -$300
    assets:broker    10 AAPL @ $30

2026-03-01 sell some
    assets:broker    -5 AAPL @ $40
    assets:cash      $200

$ hledger -f- holdings -e 2026-04-01
Holdings on 2026-03-31

               || Date  Age    Units  Avg cost  Unit price  Total cost  Total value  Weight  UGain  UGain%  RGain  XIRR 
===============++=======================================================================================================
 assets:broker ||            15 AAPL       $20                    $300                                       $100       
---------------++-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
               ||            15 AAPL       $20                    $300                                       $100       

# ** 39. With --lots, each AVERAGE lot row shows the pool's average as its
# unit cost (as in the lot state, where every pool lot carries the current
# average), not its original acquisition cost. And since all displayed lots
# here are in AVERAGE pools, the column keeps its "Avg cost" title.
$ hledger -f- holdings -e 2026-04-01 --lots
Holdings on 2026-03-31

                            ||       Date  Age    Units  Avg cost  Unit price  Total cost  Total value  Weight  UGain  UGain%  RGain  XIRR 
============================++=============================================================================================================
 assets:broker:{2026-01-01} || 2026-01-01  89d   5 AAPL       $20                    $100                                       $100       
 assets:broker:{2026-02-01} || 2026-02-01  58d  10 AAPL       $20                    $200                                                  
----------------------------++-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
                            ||                  15 AAPL       $20                    $300                                       $100       

# ** 40. The average is calculated as of the report end date: before the
# second acquisition, it is the first acquisition's cost.
$ hledger -f- holdings -e 2026-01-15
Holdings on 2026-01-14

               ||       Date  Age    Units  Avg cost  Unit price  Total cost  Total value  Weight  UGain  UGain%  RGain  XIRR 
===============++=============================================================================================================
 assets:broker || 2026-01-01  13d  10 AAPL       $10                    $100                                                  
---------------++-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
               ||                  10 AAPL       $10                    $100                                                  

# ** 41. An AVERAGEALL pool spans all accounts holding the commodity:
# each account shows the global average, not its own acquisitions' average.
<
commodity AAPL  ; lots:AVERAGEALL

2026-01-01 buy cheap at broker1
    assets:cash      -$100
    assets:broker1    10 AAPL @ $10

2026-02-01 buy dear at broker2
    assets:cash      -$300
    assets:broker2    10 AAPL @ $30

$ hledger -f- holdings -e 2026-03-01
